+# Daily Grind coffee cards
+
+`index.html` loads `coffee-card.js` as a native ES module. Each `<coffee-card>`
+owns its markup and styling in an open shadow root and inherits the site's font,
+text color, and CSS color variables.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card name="Maple Oat Latte" description="Oat milk and maple syrup."
+  href="/menu/seasonal" price="5.50" featured></coffee-card>
+```
+
+Attributes and same-named JavaScript properties reflect in both directions:
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default and behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | string | Empty string |
+| `description` | string | Empty string |
+| `href` | string | `/menu`; only HTTP(S) and relative web links are navigable |
+| `price` | number or `null` | Optional USD price; absent, blank, invalid, or negative attributes hide it |
+| `featured` | boolean | False; presence means true, including `featured="false"` |
+
+Assigning `null` or `undefined` to a string property or `price` removes its
+attribute. The `price` setter accepts finite non-negative numeric values (including
+numeric strings), throws `TypeError` for invalid values, and preserves zero.
+Set `card.featured = false` or remove the attribute to turn the badge off.
+The original menu omits prices and badges so its presentation stays the same.
+
+Changes update the existing DOM without replacing the link or losing focus.
+Properties assigned before registration are replayed through their setters when
+the element connects. Connection attaches the link's selection listener;
+disconnection removes it, and reconnection restores it. Activating the link emits
+a bubbling, composed `coffee-select` event with `{ name, href, price, featured }`
+in `event.detail`, alongside normal link navigation.
+
+Run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` followed by `pnpm test` for DOM-based automated checks. No build step
+is required.
